# Role Selection and Pursuit Priority

Operational reference: `BLUEPRINT.md` §138
(`BORA_ROLE_SELECTION_AND_PURSUIT_PRIORITY_STANDARD_V1`) locks the full
doctrine for which roles Career OS should actively search for,
prioritize, and spend application effort on. This file is a pointer, not
a restatement — read §138 (and the sections it cross-references: §5, §6,
§7, §19-21, §132, §135, §136) before acting on discovery, comparison-pool,
freshness, remote-authenticity, or pursuit-priority questions.

## Governance boundary (the one invariant worth restating here)

This doctrine governs Pursuit Truth and Package Truth only — discovery
priority, pursuit urgency, and how a serious role is presented for Bora's
decision. It never governs Qualification Truth, Employer Truth, Candidate
Truth, or Match Truth, all of which remain owned entirely by
`job_analysis.py`, `job_decision.py`, and the existing deterministic
requirement/evidence-match/qualification-gate/recruiter-threshold
pipeline, unchanged.

Do not convert, under any circumstance:

* `UNKNOWN` -> `SUPPORTED`;
* `UNKNOWN` -> `NONE`;
* adjacent experience -> direct experience;
* functional overlap -> qualification;
* good location -> qualification;
* a fresh posting -> qualification;
* remote authenticity -> qualification;
* institutional affinity -> qualification;
* network access -> qualification.

## Quick-reference vocabulary (full definitions in §138, not here)

* Comparison-pool discovery bands: A+ / A / B / C (§138.1) -- "do not
  actively target" 2-4/3-5/5+/Senior/Lead/Principal/Manager is a
  discovery/pursuit-economics rule, never an automatic qualification
  REJECT; the existing mechanical recruiter-threshold guard in
  `job_decision.py` remains authoritative and unchanged.
* Freshness bands: `VERY_FRESH` / `FRESH` / `AGING` / `STALE_LEANING` /
  `UNKNOWN` (§138.5) -- Bora-specific pursuit urgency, never a universal
  employer-hiring-probability claim, and never a modification of Employer
  Truth. `STALE_LEANING` never means closed or unqualified.
* Locked discovery windows (§138.5): `GOLD_WINDOW` = 0-7 days;
  `STRETCH_WINDOW` = 8-14 days; `FAR_STRETCH_WINDOW` = 15-21 days;
  `EXCEPTION_ONLY_WINDOW` = 22+ days; `UNKNOWN_WINDOW` when employer posting
  date is not reliable. `EXCEPTION_ONLY_WINDOW` is not a hard exclusion: an
  unusually strong, strategically exceptional, first-party verified-live role
  may still deserve pursuit. Missing/unreliable employer posting date stays
  `UNKNOWN` / `UNKNOWN_WINDOW`; never substitute `discovered_date` or
  `date_first_seen` as the employer posting date. These are governance/
  presentation labels only, never schema/runtime enums or employer cutoffs.
* Bora-facing recency visibility gate (§138.5): before serious-role surfacing
  or package work, require either a reliable employer/official-ATS posting
  date or an authoritative dated application-intake window for the exact role.
  A live Apply button, résumé-upload form, requisition shell, crawl date,
  `discovered_date`, `date_first_seen`, aggregator age, or social-platform age
  alone is insufficient. If neither recency anchor exists, suppress the role
  from Bora-facing discovery and do not package it. An exact current role state
  saying closed/expired/filled/no longer accepting applications suppresses it
  unless a newer first-party employer/official-ATS source explicitly reopens
  intake. A dated application-window rescue permits visibility without fabricating
  an employer posting date: Freshness remains `UNKNOWN` and Discovery Window remains
  `UNKNOWN_WINDOW`. Closure status never upgrades platform/aggregator age into Employer
  Truth or `board_posted_date`.
* Locked work-format preferences (§138.4): actively favor verified `REMOTE`,
  `CONTRACT`/contract-to-hire/temporary, and `PART_TIME` opportunities in
  discovery; combinations such as remote + contract or remote + part-time get
  strong tiebreak priority among otherwise comparable opportunities. Boston/
  Greater Boston contract, temporary, and part-time roles also get positive
  preference even when hybrid or onsite. These are discovery biases, not hard
  filters or a fixed Lane A/B/C hierarchy: they never override fit,
  authorization, first-party actionability, Candidate/Match/Qualification
  Truth, or suppress an unusually strong accessible full-time/hybrid/onsite
  opportunity.
* Remote authenticity: `VERIFIED` / `LIKELY_LEGITIMATE` / `UNCLEAR` /
  `HIGH_RISK` / `CONFIRMED_FRAUD` / `N/A` (§138.7) -- doctrine vocabulary
  for human/model assessment only; not a schema enum or runtime field.
* Bora-specific excluded application-route host (§138.6.1): based on
  Bora's own direct usability evidence, `massanf.taleo.net` is excluded --
  if a role's only current application route depends on it, first-party
  actionability fails and this routes through the existing §135/§138.6
  actionability consequence: `WATCH`/no serious application effort,
  unless an independent blocker already produces `REJECT`. This creates
  no new gate and does not amend §138.8; package/tailoring/application
  work for such a role remains blocked under the existing
  actionability/package gates, the same way it already is for any other
  first-party actionability failure. This does not blacklist MassDOT,
  MassCareers, Massachusetts government employers, or Taleo globally; a
  different verified working official application route may still pass.
  Remains active until Bora explicitly revokes it after a successful
  direct usability re-test. Motivating example: MassDOT -- IT Data
  Analyst I, requisition 260005JH, the cold-start failure that would now
  route to `WATCH`/no serious application effort under this doctrine.
* Bora-specific excluded employer family (§138.6.2,
  `BORA_EXCLUDED_EMPLOYER_FAMILY_V1`): Mass General Brigham system roles --
  first-party-identified, including Mass General Brigham, Massachusetts
  General Hospital / The General Hospital Corporation, Brigham and Women's
  Hospital, and other MGB-system entities a first-party source itself
  identifies -- are excluded from serious Bora-facing discovery and package
  generation. Pursuit/preference exclusion only, not a claim that Mass
  General Brigham is a bad employer, and not
  Qualification/Employer/Candidate/Match Truth. Integrated into §138.8
  serious-role promotion as a required third check alongside the §138.5
  recency visibility gate and the §138.14 start horizon gate: promotion
  requires all three to PASS, and this employer-family-exclusion check
  cannot be skipped once recency and start-horizon pass. When an excluded
  role is referenced for audit/debugging only, its reason is labeled
  `BORA_EXCLUDED_EMPLOYER`, never presented as a Qualification Truth
  REJECT; any independent REJECT from a separate blocker is preserved
  unchanged. No unsupported global MGB-affiliate list -- only
  first-party-identified entities are covered. Remains active for the
  whole employer family until Bora explicitly overrides one specific role
  or explicitly revokes the family exclusion; a per-role override does not
  revoke the family exclusion for any other MGB-system role -- it applies
  only to that one specific role. Historical Submitted Application Truth
  for any already-submitted Mass General Brigham system application is not
  rewritten.
* Discovery-source ladder (§18.1, `DISCOVERY_SOURCE_LADDER_V1` -- source-
  ladder ordering only, a distinct identifier from
  `BORA_EXCLUDED_EMPLOYER_FAMILY_V1` above, with no cross-ID coupling):
  LinkedIn Free and Brandeis Handshake are preferred first-wave discovery
  surfaces, alongside targeted direct employer/official ATS searches, for
  efficient high-signal inventory discovery. Simplify Free, Built In,
  HigherEdJobs, Idealist, staffing/recruiting firms, company lists,
  referrals, recruiter outreach, and other credible job sources remain
  valid secondary/specialized discovery channels. Generic aggregators and
  generic search/index snippet results remain the lowest-confidence tier:
  lead generation only. Discovery source and verification/application
  source remain separate; a LinkedIn/Handshake listing may justify
  checking a role but by itself never establishes Employer Truth, the
  §138.5 recency-anchor requirement, first-party actionability, or
  package-time semantic quorum -- LinkedIn/Handshake posting age alone
  cannot satisfy the §138.5 recency-anchor requirement. Serious-role
  promotion still requires the existing §138.5 recency visibility gate,
  §138.14 start horizon gate, the §138.6.2 employer-family-exclusion check
  PASS, §135/§138.6 first-party actionability, and the package-time
  first-party recheck.
* Start horizon gate (§138.14): known intended start 0-30 days from the
  current operating date = TARGETED near-term window (actively target —
  Career OS should actively seek out and prioritize discovery/application
  effort toward roles expected to start within this window); 31-60 days =
  acceptable around-target window; more than 60 days = suppress from
  Bora-facing serious discovery and package generation unless Bora
  explicitly requests a future-start pipeline or explicitly overrides the
  timing gate for that role. An unstated/unreliable start date remains
  `UNKNOWN` and is never suppressed merely because it was omitted. A near
  application deadline or recent posting never rescues a known far-future
  start. Bora-specific pursuit/discovery timing doctrine only — never
  Qualification/Employer/Candidate/Match Truth, authorization, or
  actionability. Motivating live example: Brattle — Research Analyst
  (Economics and Finance), known start July 2027, suppressed on
  2026-09-09 despite a September 14 application deadline.
* Serious-role output standard (§138.8): promotion into serious-role output
  requires passing BOTH the §138.5 recency visibility gate AND the §138.14
  start horizon gate; failing either one suppresses the role regardless of
  the other, absent an explicit Bora override of that specific gate.
  Promotion additionally requires the §138.6.2 Bora-specific
  employer-family-exclusion check to PASS as a required third check
  alongside those two gates -- this is a three-check requirement, not a
  two-check one: the employer-family-exclusion check cannot be skipped
  once the §138.5 and §138.14 gates both pass, and a role suppressed
  under it does not enter serious-role output or package generation
  regardless of its status under the other two, absent an explicit Bora
  override of that specific check per §138.6.2's own override terms. When
  an excluded role is referenced for audit/debugging only, its reason is
  labeled `BORA_EXCLUDED_EMPLOYER`, never presented as a Qualification
  Truth REJECT, and any independent REJECT from a separate blocker is
  preserved unchanged. Every
  serious role analysis presents Bora Fit, Comparison Pool,
  Freshness, Discovery Window, Location/Work Arrangement, First-Party Actionability, Remote
  Authenticity, Authorization, Opportunity Value, Pursuit Economics, and
  a Final Verdict (`PURSUE - DEEP` / `PURSUE - CONTROLLED HIGH-QUALITY` /
  `PURSUE - EFFICIENT` / `WATCH` / `REJECT`). No numeric score, no fake
  probability, no point system, ever.

**Disambiguation (§138.8):** every §138.8 label is presentation
vocabulary for Pursuit Truth only -- never a value of, or synonym for,
`Job.decision`, `Job.lane`, `role_status`, or `source_verification_status`,
and never to be written into those persisted/runtime fields (e.g.
Freshness `STALE_LEANING` != `role_status=POSSIBLY_STALE`; Final Verdict
`WATCH`/`REJECT` do not redefine the existing `Job.decision` enum even
where the label text coincides).

## Stop rule

This doctrine lock does not itself authorize runtime implementation --
no new schema, enum, runtime scoring, lane value, decision value,
database field, remote-fraud classifier, automated fraud declaration, or
job-search automation change is pre-authorized by §138. A separate,
explicitly earned architecture audit under §133's build-economy gate is
required before any of that is built.
